---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal title="Privacy policy" description="What personal data this site collects, why, and your rights.">
  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <p>The controller of personal data collected through this site is {site.author.name}, {site.author.city}. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

  <h2>What is collected and why</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Purchases</strong> — name, email address, country and the amount paid, received from Stripe after checkout. Used to deliver the file, issue the download link, send the receipt and keep the records tax law requires. Stripe processes your card details under its own privacy policy; they never reach this site.</li>
    <li><strong>Download links</strong> — the purchase identifier and the time a link was issued and used, so that a link can be reissued and a leaked one revoked.</li>
    <li><strong>Release notifications</strong> — your email address, if you ask to be told when a new guide ships. Used for that one message per guide and nothing else; every message carries an unsubscribe link.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact form</strong> — name, email and the text of your message. Used only to answer you, kept only in the mailbox.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics (Google Analytics 4)</strong> — analytics cookies are set only after you consent in the cookie banner. Without consent only anonymous, cookie-less signals are sent (Google Consent Mode). Details are in the <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Personal data is not sold and is not shared with third parties for marketing.</p>

  <h2>Where data is processed</h2>
  <p>The site runs on Cloudflare infrastructure; payments are processed by Stripe; emails are sent through Cloudflare. Each is bound by a data-processing agreement.</p>

  <h2>How long</h2>
  <p>Purchase records are kept for as long as tax law requires (currently ten years in Bulgaria). Notification addresses are kept until you unsubscribe. Contact correspondence is kept as long as it is needed to answer you; deletion can be requested at any time.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to access, correct, delete and restrict the processing of your data, to object, and to lodge a complaint with the Bulgarian Commission for Personal Data Protection (CPDP) or your local authority. Requests go to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
